<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fernando Villavicencio</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1963">1963</a>–<a href="/years/2023">2023</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fernando Villavicencio was an Ecuadorian investigative journalist and politician who exposed corruption in the oil sector and under the government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rafael-correa">Rafael Correa</a>. As a member of the National Assembly and presidential candidate in 2023, he campaigned against organised crime. He was shot dead after a campaign rally in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quito">Quito</a> on 9 August 2023, days before the election.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fernando-villavicencio.jpg" alt="Fernando Villavicencio" width="320" height="398" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Asamblea Nacional del Ecuador from QUito, Ecuador · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fernando_Villavicencio_2023.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
